.\" sliverctl(1). Source of truth for commands: crates/sliverctl/src/cli.rs (a test keeps this
.\" page in sync with `sliverctl help`).
.TH SLIVERCTL 1 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliverctl \- control the Touch Bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliverctl
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B sliverctl config
.I subcommand
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliverctl
talks to
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
over its session D\-Bus interface
.RI ( io.github.wawow830.Sliver ,
.BR Control1 ).
It can inspect the bar and drive it the way
.B pkill \-RTMIN+N waybar
drives waybar.
.PP
The
.B config
commands work offline: they edit the configuration file
(see
.BR sliver\-config (5))
and never touch D\-Bus.
The agent picks the change up by itself.
.PP
.I MODULE
is any module id:
a built\-in
.RB ( clock ,
.BR battery#bat2 ),
or a user module
.RB ( custom/vpn ).
.SH INSPECTING
.TP
.B status
Agent health, active layer and profile, the layout on the bar and why
(the rule that picked it, the layer default, or forced by
.BR layout ),
and the agent's current config, stylesheet and module errors (one per line), if any.
.TP
.B modules
Every module on the bar: its id, key, type, layer, classes, x and width.
.TP
.RB "\fBdoctor\fR [" \-\-json ]
Check the whole install, reading only: whether sliverd and tiny\-dfr are running (and not both),
the agent's health and errors, the configuration, whether the desktop says which window has
focus, and the services that feed modules (NetworkManager, UPower,
logind, a notification daemon, xdg\-desktop\-portal, PipeWire).
Each line is ok, WARN (a module will be empty) or FAIL (the bar or config isn't working), with the
fix under it.
The machine, OS and desktop are printed first, so the output can go into a bug report.
The exit status is 1 if anything failed.
.B \-\-json
prints the same as one JSON object.
Run it inside the desktop session.
.SH CONTROLLING
.TP
.B reload
Reload the configuration.
Errors are printed, and the exit status is 1 if there are any.
An invalid configuration is never applied.
.TP
.BI validate " file"
Check a configuration file without applying it; the same as
.BI "config check " file\fR.
.TP
.BI signal " n"
Re\-run every module configured with
.BI "signal = " n\fR.
.B RTMIN+\fIn\fR
is accepted too.
.TP
.BI refresh " module"
Re\-run one module now.
.TP
.BI show " module\fR, " hide " module\fR, " toggle " module"
Change a module's visibility until the agent restarts.
The configuration file isn't touched.
.TP
.B reset\-visibility
Undo every
.BR show ,
.B hide
and
.BR toggle .
.TP
.BI tap " module\fR, " hold " module\fR, " double\-tap " module"
Fire the module's binding for that gesture, as if it had been touched.
.TP
.BI trigger " module gesture"
The same for any gesture:
.BR tap ,
.BR hold ,
.BR double\-tap ,
.BR swipe\-left ,
.BR swipe\-right .
.TP
.BI update " module key" = "value ..."
Push output to a custom module that has no
.BR exec ,
using the keys a script would print:
.BR text ,
.BR icon ,
.BR class ,
.BR percentage ,
.BR alt ,
.BR tooltip .
.TP
.BI "layer switch" " name"
Make
.I name
the current layer.
.TP
.BI "layer push" " name \fR[\fPtimeout-ms\fR]"
Open a layer on top, optionally closing it again after
.IR timeout\-ms .
.TP
.B layer pop
Close the top layer.
.TP
.BI "layer toggle" " name"
Open the layer, or close it if it is open.
.TP
.BI layout " name"
Force a layout until the context changes.
.TP
.BI profile " name"
Switch to another profile (see
.BR sliver\-config (5)).
The agent refuses a profile that doesn't validate and keeps the current one.
.TP
.BR bar " " show | hide | toggle
Blank or restore the whole bar.
The safe hatch (press Fn twice and hold) still works while the bar is hidden.
.TP
.BI "var set" " name value"
Set a user variable, usable in rule conditions.
.TP
.BR render " [" \-\-config
.IR file ]
.BR \-o | \-\-output
.I out.png
Save what the bar shows now as PNG, or, with
.BR \-\-config ,
how it would look with that configuration (drawn with the live state, as if saved over the
current configuration; the bar itself doesn't change).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B sliverctl config
edits the user configuration file.
Comments are kept, and an edit that would make the configuration invalid is refused.
.TP
.B config path
Where sliver looks for its configuration.
The file in use is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BR "config check " [ \fIfile\fP ]
Parse and validate.
The exit status is 1 if there are errors.
.TP
.BI "config get" " key"
For example
.B modules.clock.format
or
.BR rules[0].layout .
.TP
.BI "config set" " key value"
.I value
is TOML
.RB ( 8 ,
.BR true ,
.BR """x""" ,
.BR "{ key = ""F1"" }" )
or a bare string.
.TP
.BI "config unset" " key"
Remove a key.
.TP
.BR "config resolve " [ \fIlayer\fP "] [" \fIctx\fP = \fIvalue\fP ...]
Show which layout and modules would be on the bar in a given context, for example
.BR "app_id=foot locked=true" .
.TP
.BR "config profile " [ list ]
List profiles; the active one is marked with
.BR * .
.B default
is
.BR config.toml .
.TP
.BI "config profile use" " name"
Make
.I name
the active profile without asking the agent; a running agent follows.
.TP
.BR "config profile new " \fIname\fP " [" \-\-from " \fIprofile\fP]"
Create a profile: your main configuration plus its own changes, or a copy of
.IR profile .
.TP
.BI "config profile rename" " old new"
.TQ
.BI "config profile rm" " name"
Rename or delete a profile.
Deleting the active one switches to
.BR default .
.SH VALUES
In
.IR key = value
arguments,
.B true
and
.B false
are booleans, integers are 32\-bit integers, decimals are doubles, and anything else is a string.
Prefix a value with
.B s:
to force a string
.RB ( text=s:42 ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the agent reports an error or isn't running, and 2 for usage errors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus to use.
.SH EXAMPLES
waybar\-style control:
.PP
.EX
sliverctl signal 8
sliverctl update custom/status text='deploy ok' class=ok
sliverctl layer push media 5000
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5),
.BR sliverd (8),
.BR busctl (1)
